<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Drogön Chögyal Phagpa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1235">1235</a>–1280</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Drogön Chögyal Phagpa was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhist</a> lama of the Sakya school who became imperial preceptor to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> he was given authority over Buddhist affairs and over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, and he devised the 'Phags-pa script, intended as a common writing system for the empire's languages.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/drogon-chogyal-phagpa.jpg" alt="Drogön Chögyal Phagpa" width="192" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chogyal.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
